Spec: Tools

Purpose:
  Scripts for building releases, regenerating map styles, fetching iOS builds, demo ride data
    and store graphics.

Owns:
  ./build_release.sh
  ./build_map_styles.dart
  ./ios_fetch_build.sh
  ./ios_screenshots.sh
  ./ios_screen_text.swift
  ./render_store_graphics.sh
  ./build_app_icons.py
  ./render_ios_store_graphics.sh
  ./check_raw_sql.py
  ./demo_rides

References:
  /docs/android-release.md
  /docs/ios-sideloading.md
  /docs/app-store.md
  /docs/specs/history/19-openfreemap.md

Must:
  `build_release.sh` builds the Play bundle, refuses a bundle not signed by `CN=Valijuu` and stores it as
    `release/retrail-<version>.aab`.
  `build_map_styles.dart` regenerates `/assets/map` from OpenFreeMap Liberty and Dark and fails when a
    layer it recolours no longer exists upstream.
  `ios_fetch_build.sh` pulls a green CI build to `~/Downloads/retrail-ios/` and can install it on a connected iPhone.
  `ios_screenshots.sh` runs only on a macOS runner (`ios-screenshots.yml`), takes App Store shots in a 6.9" iPhone
    simulator and fails when a shot is not `1320 x 2868` px. It seeds the app's preferences as a plist file
    in the app container while the simulator is shut down, and fails when the text in the home shot
    (`ios_screen_text.swift`, Vision OCR) is not the home screen in the shot's language with rides.
    The other motives come from `/integration_test/store_screenshots_test.dart` (provider overrides,
    replayed demo GPS, no Live Activity): it prints `RETRAIL_SHOT <name>`, the script takes the shot with
    `simctl io screenshot` and acks with a file in the app's Documents. The script fails when a motive's
    shot is missing, has the wrong size or lacks its expected text in the shot's language.
  `build_app_icons.py` lifts the R off the dark tile of the logo source and writes the branding PNGs, the Android splash icon and
    status-bar glyph and the iOS Live Activity mark; `dart run flutter_launcher_icons` then writes the launcher icons.
  `render_store_graphics.sh` renders the icon, feature graphics and framed screenshots at 2x, scaled down with Lanczos.
  `render_ios_store_graphics.sh` frames the Simulator shots for the App Store (1320 x 2868) the same way: caption, phone, optional second phone (light + dark) and an enlarged excerpt, listed in `store/ios/screenshots.tsv`.
  Demo rides contain invented routes only.
  `check_raw_sql.py` fails when a Drift `custom*` call (`customSelect`, `customStatement`, `customUpdate`,
    `customInsert`, `customWriteReturning`) gets SQL that is not a plain literal (`$`, `+`, a variable).
    It runs in `.githooks/pre-commit`. An exception needs `// sql-ok: <reason>` on the call line.

Tasks:
  [x] #87 Run `ios-screenshots.yml` once and fix what breaks (simulator names, prefs seeding, DB path, map load time).
  [x] #87 Capture the other motives with `integration_test/store_screenshots_test.dart`.
